Complete Feature Checklist for a Website Development & SEO Agency
For your agency, which handles website development, SEO, cold email outreach, and web-related digital marketing, you need a system that manages the entire business — from finding a prospect without a website to signing the client, delivering the project, collecting payments, and renewing the contract.
Since you're planning a two-person agency, with one person managing clients and sales and the other handling website development and SEO, I'd organize the features into the following modules. You can use this as a master requirements list for your Notion CRM or a future custom agency management platform.
1. The complete agency system
01. Lead generation & prospect database
Find businesses that need websites or SEO and organize their contact information.
02. Cold email marketing & follow-ups
Manage outreach campaigns, replies, deliverability, follow-up schedules and booked meetings.
03. Sales CRM & deal management
Track calls, proposals, quotations, negotiations, and signed contracts.
04. Website & SEO project delivery
Manage website builds, SEO tasks, approvals, deadlines, and ongoing optimization.
05. Billing, subscriptions & renewals
Track revenue, invoices, expenses, recurring fees, overdue payments, and renewal dates.
06. Reporting, automation & agency dashboard
Monitor business performance, client results, team workload, and upcoming actions.
