Rescheduling
Let the prospect change or cancel a booking and update the calendar accordingly.
CRM synchronization
Create or update the lead, associate the meeting, and assign a follow-up task.
Meeting outcomes
Track attended, no-show, rescheduled, qualified, proposal requested and not interested.
Recommended booking flow
Visitor clicks “Book a Call”
Select meeting type and available time
Enter contact and project details
Confirm booking and create calendar event
Send confirmation, reminder and CRM update
A practical starting option is Calendly or Cal.com integrated with your calendar and CRM. Check current plans and integration limits before choosing.
6. SEO: all the features your agency website needs
There are two different SEO requirements:
SEO for your own agency website: helps potential customers find you through Google and other search engines.
SEO services for your clients: the work your agency sells and delivers.
Your own website needs both technical foundations and a content strategy.
A. Technical SEO
Crawlable pages and a logical URL structure.
XML sitemap that updates when relevant pages change.
Correct robots.txt directives.
Canonical tags to avoid duplicate URL problems.
Correct HTTP status codes and redirects.
HTTPS and secure page delivery.
Mobile-friendly, responsive layouts.
Fast loading and good Core Web Vitals.
Clean internal linking and breadcrumb navigation where useful.
Correct indexing and no accidental blocking of important pages.
Custom 404 page and broken-link checks.
Image compression, responsive image sizes and descriptive alt text.
Structured data that accurately describes page content.
Consistent preferred domain and URL format.
Pagination and filter handling where relevant.
A staging site protected from search indexing.
Monitoring for unexpected indexing or server errors.
